# Perchance capture output is LF; keep it that way regardless of core.autocrlf.
#
# Added 2026-08-14. This repo had no .gitattributes at all until then, which surfaced when the
# srcManifest backfill committed 14 files and git warned that LF would become CRLF on the next
# checkout for every one of them. `generators` has carried this rule since 2026-08-10; this repo
# was split out of it on 2026-08-11 and the file did not come along.
#
# This is not only a tidiness rule. Every file under a slug's src/ has a byte size declared in
# that slug's meta.json srcManifest, and that declared size is the only integrity check this repo
# has -- it is what proves a capture downloaded a whole file rather than a truncated one. A CRLF
# conversion changes the byte size of every text file it touches and would break that check
# repo-wide, turning the one available proof of completeness into noise.
#
# That matters more here than in `generators`, because top-down-rpg-template is 404 on perchance
# and this repo holds the only copy of it that exists. There is nothing to re-fetch it from if a
# checkout mangles it.
*.txt           text eol=lf
*.json          text eol=lf
*.md            text eol=lf
*.js            text eol=lf
*.pjs           text eol=lf
*.html          text eol=lf
*.css           text eol=lf
*.ts            text eol=lf
*.jsx           text eol=lf
LICENSE         text eol=lf
.gitattributes  text eol=lf

# Binary srcManifest payloads -- srcManifest declares sizes for these too, so any conversion
# corrupts both the file and the check. Marked explicitly rather than left to auto-detection.
*.png           binary
*.jpg           binary
*.jpeg          binary
*.zip           binary
